Z||000001||theogre||10-18-2000||07:28 PM||||read the door notes in my cave. should cover most of it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||10-18-2000||07:31 PM||||You have to take the inner panel off.  Then the little triangular rubber piece at the front of the door so that you can remove the mirror.  There are 7 (I think) torx headed screws along the front and back edges of the inside of the door.  Pry up the moulding under the outer door handle (the long piece of moulding, leave the little 2-3" piece in place) and remove the entire moulding.  Be very careful with the clips that hold it in place.  Remove two hex head screws under the moulding.  Pry out the 4 plastic rivets on the very bottom of the skin.  There is a pushrod that attaches from the door lock to the mechanism in the door that must be carefully removed.  Don't remove the lock or the outer handle.  <P>There may be a better explanation at Ogre's Cave -- link is at the bottom of this (and every) page.<P>Looks like Ogre beat me to it!!<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 10-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||baldlobo||10-18-2000||07:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>read the door notes in my cave. should cover most of it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>thanks||||reg||1
